{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123217","id":4449485970,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCTXEkg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123217","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123217.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123217.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123217","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123217/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123217/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123217/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d3f63bc864663a99b87e43a9a5cec327aeb7ef2d","number":123217,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Physics: Preserve RigidBody2D/3D scale during physics sync","user":{"login":"NAVEENKUMARKR777","id":165763161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCeFYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165763161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777","html_url":"https://github.com/NAVEENKUMARKR777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #5734\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`RigidBody2D`/`RigidBody3D::_sync_body_state()` applies the physics engine's\r\ncomputed transform directly via `set_global_transform()`. That transform only\r\ncarries rotation and position — physics simulation has no concept of the\r\nnode's own visual scale — so any scale set on the node (uniform or not) was\r\nsilently reset to `(1, 1)` / `(1, 1, 1)` on the very next physics tick.\r\n\r\n**Fix**: cache the node's scale (and skew, for the 2D case, since\r\n`Transform2D`'s basis isn't pure rotation+scale) right before applying the\r\nphysics transform, then restore it via the existing `set_scale()`/`set_skew()`\r\nsetters, which already know how to recombine a fresh rotation with a\r\npreserved scale/skew.\r\n\r\n**Scope**: this only fixes the *visual* symptom (the node's own transform\r\nsnapping back). Collision response is unaffected and continues to be driven\r\nentirely by the scale of the body's own child `CollisionShape2D`/`3D` nodes,\r\nindependent of the body's transform sync — this was already a separate,\r\ncorrect code path. Making the collision *shape* itself scale-aware (affecting\r\nmass/inertia) is a much larger change and out of scope here; the editor\r\nconfiguration warning is reworded to make this distinction clear rather than\r\nclaim scale is simply \"overridden.\"\r\n\r\n**Testing**: verified manually with a headless scene — a `RigidBody3D` scaled\r\n`(1, 3, 1)` and a `RigidBody2D` scaled `(1, 3)` both held their scale across\r\n5 physics ticks with this fix (both would previously reset to `(1,1,1)`/\r\n`(1,1)` on the first tick). I did not add an automated regression test for\r\nthis, since it requires a running physics simulation across multiple ticks,\r\nwhich doesn't fit the existing headless-doctest test infrastructure well —\r\nhappy to add a scene-based test if reviewers want one, or take pointers on\r\nthe preferred way to test this in-tree.\r\n\r\n**AI disclosure**: This change (root-cause analysis, implementation, and\r\nmanual verification) was developed with Claude (Anthropic), directed and\r\nreviewed by me. I read and understand the diff before submitting it.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T07:53:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T10:46:56Z","closed_at":"2026-09-07T10:46:50Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6eae8abca1cf020f8cb9f88d7182a9cf0e3c7ace","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"NAVEENKUMARKR777:fix/rigidbody-scale-reset","ref":"fix/rigidbody-scale-reset","repo":{"id":1357859302,"node_id":"R_kgDOUO9J5g","name":"godot","full_name":"NAVEENKUMARKR777/godot","owner":{"login":"NAVEENKUMARKR777","id":165763161,"node_id":"U_kgDOCeFYWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165763161?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777","html_url":"https://github.com/NAVEENKUMARKR777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NAVEENKUMARKR777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.gi